    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 full suite reports `Tests run: 23, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment for `POST /api/owners`, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where YY is the last two digits of the registration year:\n\n1. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignMembershipNumber.java`: reads the `@Val Owner`, computes `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, floorMod(year, 100))`, and sets it in place. It's derived purely from the owner's own fields (seed-independent), matching the existing `Assign*` step conventions.\n\n3. **Endpoint wiring** \u2014 inserted `assignMembershipNumber` into `owners.POST.yml` right after `assignCustomerCode` (so `customerCode` is set) and after `build` (so `registrationDate` is set), under the same `transaction` governance, flowing into `assignHousehold`.\n\n4. **Response DTO** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` property to the generated `OwnerDto` via `openapi.yml`; MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n\n5. **Schemas** \u2014 added the `membership_number` column to the h2, hsqldb, mysql, and postgres `schema.sql` files.\n\nThe new `Cp14Tests.coreMembershipNumberFormat` passes, as does the entire existing suite.",
